# The GitHub proxy's token. Server-side only — Vite never exposes it, because
# it has no VITE_ prefix and the proxy runs as a serverless function, not in
# the browser.
#
# A FINE-GRAINED token with "Public repositories (read-only)" is sufficient.
# It does not need any account scope: the proxy only reads public profiles,
# public repository lists and public READMEs.
#
# Set this in the Vercel dashboard, not in a committed file.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional: point the client somewhere other than the built-in proxy.
# Leave unset in normal use.
# VITE_GITHUB_API=
